+When a gesture should keep the drawing's existing bend side, the same helper's `transported_pole` carries that side with the moving shoulder–wrist axis. A fixed world-space pole can cross the axis and flip an elbow. A deliberate reversal still needs a designed pose/view transition. Check wrist orientation as part of the whole chain: revise the pose or add matching artwork if a prop tilt requires an implausible wrist. Preserve the intended action and timing, rather than silently suppressing movement to pass a check.
